WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:12.350
What up yo? This week we flowin
with our boy with Mark Twain’s Adventures

00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:18.890
of Huckleberry Finn.
Huck Finn and his main man Tom

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:23.720
Sawyer sittin FAT after their last adventure,
but nxow Huck gotta live with some crusty

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:28.930
ol widow who tryin to “civilize” him.
When Huck’s boozed-up daddy Pap swangs in

00:00:28.930 --> 00:00:34.870
to town, he snatches up Huck to live in his
stuffy-ass digs and try to swipe all his cheddar.

00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:39.120
Sick of gettin his ass whooped erry time Pap
sips too much crunk juice,

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:44.570
Huck decide to fake his own murder and lay
low on Jackson’s Island while the laws patrollin.

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:49.440
After chillin a couple days on the
island, Huck hooks up with Jim, a slave he

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:54.739
know from the hood, who dun split after hearin
his ass bout to get sold. Since they both

00:00:54.739 --> 00:00:58.670
duckin the 5-0, they decide to team up and
skip town.

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:02.489
When our boys get separated, Huck finds himself
at the phat crib of

00:01:02.489 --> 00:01:07.070
the Grangerfords, a family who been beefin
wit another crew called the Shepherdsons fo

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:11.710
generations. Deez fools can’t even remember
why they’re bustin caps in eachother. Huck

00:01:11.710 --> 00:01:15.950
straight flips when his boy Buck Grangerford
get iced over some bullsh**.

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:20.459
Then Huck and Jim rescue two shady
thugs named the Duke and King as they runnin

00:01:20.459 --> 00:01:23.280
from the fuzz.
These fools sliding from town to

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:28.929
town straight hustlin homies fo their paper.
Eventually, these shysters get REAL dirty

00:01:28.929 --> 00:01:33.369
and sell Jim to a bunch of plantation owning
crackas named The Phelps.

00:01:33.369 --> 00:01:37.649
Huck slides over to da Phelps spot
to free Jim when a woman say “Yo wassap

00:01:37.649 --> 00:01:43.250
Tom!?” Tom? Turns out, these cats are Tom
Sawyer’s aunt and uncle and they think Huck

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:49.119
is Tom. When Tom actually shows up, Tom tells
Huck to play it cool and Tom pretends to be

00:01:49.119 --> 00:01:52.450
his kid brutha Sid.
Tom comes up with a plan to bust

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:57.229
him out like it some kind of prison break.
But just as they bout to split, Tom gets capped

00:01:57.229 --> 00:02:02.940
in the leg and Jim gets GOT again.
Next morning, Tom all like: “Look,

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:09.090
brah. Jim was actually a free man this whole
time. So that escape plan? I was just playin.”

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:12.970
The hell?! A brother’s freedom ain’t no
game.

00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:17.239
So Huck and Jim part ways and Tom’s aunt
offers to adopt Huck. but Huck

00:02:17.239 --> 00:02:24.239
done with all this “sivil” nonsense, so
he decide to start trekkin to some new turf.

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:31.500
Open up yo ears and get ready for
some truth, son! By far da most throwed-up

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:36.170
symbol up in here is the Mississippi river.
See, the river representin’ freedom-

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:41.209
not only Jim’s freedom from slavery, but
freedom from all the crooked sh** always goin

00:02:41.209 --> 00:02:44.890
down in the “civilized” world.
But at the same time, the river

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:49.780
also reppin’ destiny. Cuz it’s the river
doin all the shot calling: where they goin,

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:54.370
when they gonna get there, and what kind of
jacked up sh** they gonna find along the way.

00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:58.390
Now even though Huck thinks all dat mess is
whack, it ain’t no thang to

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:02.010
all dem “civilized” peeps Huck dealin
with. And as the only brutha who keepin it

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:05.719
real enough to see through society’s bullsh**-
he gets mad lonely.

00:03:05.719 --> 00:03:09.450
Sparky reads quote: “When it was dark I
set by my camp fire smoking, and feeling pretty

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:14.810
satisfied; but by and by it got sort of lonesome,
and so I went and set on the bank and listened

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:19.989
to the currents washing along, and counted
the stars and drift-logs and rafts that come

00:03:19.989 --> 00:03:23.010
down” (51)
Only when Huck gets to know Jim

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:28.079
does he find someone he can chill with. And
to Jim, ain’t nobody ever had his back like

00:03:28.079 --> 00:03:31.569
Huck. Dat raft becomes the realest home Huck
ever known.

00:03:31.569 --> 00:03:35.939
Cuz when he on the shore, Huck
seein stupid sh** go down on the reg- hoods

00:03:35.939 --> 00:03:41.129
talkin bout glockin eachother, families icing
kids for no good reason, and his own daddy

00:03:41.129 --> 00:03:44.670
slappin him up. On the real, people people
can be dicks, man.

00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:48.389
And what’s mad ironic is dat even though
Huck ain’t educated, don’t

00:03:48.389 --> 00:03:53.510
buy in to no religious jive, and don’t consider
himself to be “civilized,” he the only

00:03:53.510 --> 00:03:59.060
cat who wise to all the backwards-ass nonsense
of a culture that accepts all this- and worst

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:02.810
of all: slavery.
So when Tom’s aunt offers Huck a

00:04:02.810 --> 00:04:07.749
place to crash fo good, he says “naw shawty.
I’m straight.” Huck don’t wanna be a

00:04:07.749 --> 00:04:11.769
part of the “civilized” world. He’d
rather take his chances and slide to a new

00:04:11.769 --> 00:04:15.629
spot where he can create a better one.
And the first step to making it a

00:04:15.629 --> 00:04:20.310
better world is by hitting subscribe. Peace,
my well-read ballas.

